 "notes": "- Task: grasp red_cube and hold it \u22655 cm above the table. Perception is noisy (~1 cm pos, several deg yaw) and every observe() is a fresh sample, so I average 6 readings per estimate (\u2192 ~4 mm std) and average yaw in 4\u00b7angle space to respect the cube's 90\u00b0 symmetry wrap at \u00b1\u03c0/4.\n- Grip force/mass/friction vary a lot, so grasping can fail or the cube can slip during the lift: verify with robot.holding() after grasp and after lift, and retry the whole sense\u2192approach\u2192grasp cycle up to 4 times (re-sensing each attempt in case the cube was pushed).\n- Approach plan: open fingers, move to (x, y, 0.08) aligned to cube yaw, descend slowly (0.05 m/s) to tool z=0.015 (pads around cube middle, fingertips 2.5 mm above table, safely under the 30 N limit), grasp, then lift straight up to tool z=0.10 so the cube bottom sits ~8.5 cm up with margin over the 5 cm bar.\n- All moves that could be out of reach are wrapped in `except Exception` (MotionError isn't importable), with a home() fallback; never hard-code positions \u2014 everything comes from observe().",
